---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../../consts';
import { getInsightBySlug, buildArticleJsonLd } from '../../../data/insights';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const post = getInsightBySlug('measuring-csr-impact-framework')!;
const articleJsonLd = buildArticleJsonLd(post, SITE.url);
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Measuring CSR Impact: A Practical Framework | Causewave"
  description={post.description}
  ogTitle="CSR Impact Measurement Framework"
  ogDescription="Build credible M&E frameworks for CSR: baseline, indicators, data collection, and learning loops that boards and regulators can trust."
  canonicalPath={post.path}
  activePage="insights"
  ogType="article"
  breadcrumbLabel={post.shortTitle}
  breadcrumbParent={{ name: 'Insights', path: 'insights/' }}
  jsonLd={articleJsonLd}
>
  <main>
    <section class="bg-slate-900 text-white section">
      <div class="max-w-screen-2xl mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <a href={`${base}insights/`} class="inline-flex items-center text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition-colors mb-6">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-2" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" /></svg>
            Back to Insights
          </a>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="text-xs font-medium text-emerald-400 bg-emerald-400/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full">{post.category}</span>
            <span class="text-xs text-slate-500">{post.dateLabel}</span>
          </div>
          <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">{post.title}</h1>
          <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300 text-lg">{post.excerpt}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="section max-w-screen-2xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6 text-lg">
          Impact measurement is no longer a “nice to have” for CSR. Boards want assurance that statutory spend creates real change; communities deserve programmes that improve over time; and implementing partners need feedback loops that go beyond annual PDFs. This framework is deliberately practical — light enough for mid-size portfolios, rigorous enough for board packs.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4">Why M&amp;E matters for CSR</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Section 135 compliance focuses on spend, policy, and disclosure (see our
          <a href={`${base}insights/csr-compliance-companies-act-2013/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">Companies Act CSR compliance guide</a>).
          Measurement goes further: it shows whether the portfolio is working, where to reallocate budget, and how to tell a credible impact story without exaggeration.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Healthcare CSR is a common stress test for M&amp;E because service volume is high and outcomes take time. Design notes live in
          <a href={`${base}insights/impactful-csr-programs-healthcare/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">healthcare CSR program design</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4">The 4-step M&amp;E framework</h2>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">1. Baseline assessment</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Before launch, document the starting state for the people and places you intend to serve. Baselines can be secondary data (district health stats, school enrolment) plus a light primary sample when secondary data is stale or too coarse. Without a baseline, “improvement” is storytelling, not measurement.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-600 mb-6">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 mt-2 shrink-0"></span><span>Define the unit of analysis (village, facility, school, household).</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 mt-2 shrink-0"></span><span>Capture 3–7 priority indicators only — not a research study.</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 mt-2 shrink-0"></span><span>Record data sources, dates, and known biases.</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">2. Indicator design</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Separate <strong>outputs</strong> (what you delivered) from <strong>outcomes</strong> (what changed). Boards often over-index on outputs because they move quickly; outcomes are slower but more honest.
        </p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
          <table class="w-full text-sm text-left border border-slate-200">
            <thead class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-700">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3">Type</th>
                <th class="p-3">Example (health)</th>
                <th class="p-3">Example (education)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="text-slate-600">
              <tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Output</td><td class="p-3">Camps held; doses administered</td><td class="p-3">Students enrolled in bridge course</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-t bg-slate-50"><td class="p-3">Quality</td><td class="p-3">Cold-chain compliance rate</td><td class="p-3">Sessions delivered as planned</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">Outcome</td><td class="p-3">Coverage in hard-to-reach pockets</td><td class="p-3">Learning level improvement</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-t bg-slate-50"><td class="p-3">Sustainability</td><td class="p-3">Facility continues protocol post-exit</td><td class="p-3">School owns remedial process</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">3. Data collection</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Prefer simple digital tools that field teams will actually use. Train once, sample quality-check monthly, and keep definitions in a one-page indicator dictionary. Integrate with partner systems where possible instead of creating a parallel universe of spreadsheets.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-600 mb-6">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 mt-2 shrink-0"></span><span>Operational data: weekly or monthly (activity and coverage).</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 mt-2 shrink-0"></span><span>Outcome data: mid-line / end-line or annual, depending on programme length.</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 mt-2 shrink-0"></span><span>Qualitative stories: structured, with consent, linked to indicators — not standalone PR.</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">4. Reporting and learning</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Reporting without learning is compliance theatre. Schedule quarterly portfolio reviews: what worked, what failed, what to stop, what to scale. Board reports should show spend vs plan, indicator trends vs baseline, risks, and decisions taken. Annual CSR disclosures then become a summary of a living system — not a scramble for numbers in March.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4">Minimum viable M&amp;E for a new CSR project</h2>
        <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-slate-600 mb-8">
          <li>One-page theory of change</li>
          <li>Baseline snapshot for primary geography</li>
          <li>5 core indicators with definitions</li>
          <li>Monthly operational dashboard</li>
          <li>Quarterly learning note + annual impact brief</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="mt-12 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 border">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Need help building CSR M&amp;E that boards trust?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
            Causewave designs measurement systems alongside programme delivery.
            Explore <a href={`${base}services/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">impact and strategy services</a> or contact us.
          </p>
          <a href={`${base}contact/`} class="mt-4 inline-flex btn btn-primary px-6 py-2 text-sm">Get in Touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
